 502:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/tasks.c **** /* Context switches are held pending while the scheduler is suspended.  Also,
 503:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/tasks.c ****  * interrupts must not manipulate the xStateListItem of a TCB, or any of the
 504:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/tasks.c ****  * lists the xStateListItem can be referenced from, if the scheduler is suspended.
 505:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/tasks.c ****  * If an interrupt needs to unblock a task while the scheduler is suspended then it
 506:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/tasks.c ****  * moves the task's event list item into the xPendingReadyList, ready for the
 507:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/tasks.c ****  * kernel to move the task from the pending ready list into the real ready list
 508:middleware/FreeRTOS-Kernel/tasks.c ****  * when the scheduler is unsuspended.  The pending ready list itself can only be
